From c06e9101b3424e32375ba765670b044a539974c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:33:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 165/187] net: omci: own GPON control-plane lifecycle

Do not tie GPON activation and the OMCC transport to ndo_open and
ndo_stop of the data netdev. Add an explicit provider lifecycle to
net/omci and let the Airoha OMCI provider acquire a dedicated GDM2/QDMA
control-plane reference.

Keep PLOAM, OMCI RX/TX and the provisioned service state alive while
userspace cycles pon0. The netdev callbacks now only expose or hide the
carrier state already computed by the GPON and OMCI control planes.

Stop and drain the OMCI transport before detaching the OAM RX handler so
provider removal cannot race a late GPON OAM descriptor.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
